1
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:08,375
Load a synthetic microscope image from local storage.

2
00:00:08,375 --> 00:00:11,750
Define two pixels per micrometre in the native scale dialog.

3
00:00:11,750 --> 00:00:15,125
Enter um so area measurements use calibrated units.

4
00:00:15,125 --> 00:00:18,500
The image now spans 256 × 200 micrometres.

5
00:00:18,500 --> 00:00:22,875
Use ImageJ's threshold preview to select bright objects.

6
00:00:22,875 --> 00:00:26,250
Specify the lower threshold of 100; the upper limit is 255.

7
00:00:26,250 --> 00:00:30,125
Apply the explicit threshold before measuring particles.

8
00:00:30,125 --> 00:00:33,500
Open the native particle-analysis controls.

9
00:00:33,500 --> 00:00:36,875
Keep particles between 50 and 500 square micrometres.

10
00:00:36,875 --> 00:00:40,250
Set circularity between 0.50 and 1.00.

11
00:00:40,250 --> 00:00:44,125
Exclude edge objects and request numbered outlines and a summary.

12
00:00:44,125 --> 00:00:49,500
The analysis produces 20 numbered particle outlines.

13
00:00:49,500 --> 00:00:54,875
The Summary table reports Count = 20, matching the test input.

14
00:00:54,875 --> 00:00:58,750
Review the individual calibrated particle areas.

15
00:00:58,750 --> 00:01:02,125
Export the measurement table as a local CSV file.

16
00:01:02,125 --> 00:01:05,500
Save the CSV before exporting the numbered outlines.

17
00:01:05,500 --> 00:01:09,375
Export the numbered outlines as a local TIFF image.

18
00:01:09,375 --> 00:01:13,750
The measurement CSV and outline TIFF are now saved.

19
00:01:13,750 --> 00:01:19,125
Inspect the calibrated measurements beside the numbered objects.
